ur normal show follow Adriana The  Sopranos in a mobsters series that's  filled with gruesome murders none was  more tragic than the death of adriana la  cerva played by dre de Matteo adriana is  a good person who just wants to escape  into witness protection with her  boyfriend Christopher  but Christopher betrays her which she  realizes at the same time the audience  doesn't her heart-wrenching final scene  it was so brutal that some fans tried to  find hope in the fact that  driana was off-camera when Silvio pulled  the trigger could it be that like Tony  Soprano she's not really dead Joyce  summers Buffy the Vampire Slayer after  being ill for most of the fifth season  Buffy's mother Joyce is finally starting  to get better but then Buffy returns  home to find her mother motionless on  the couch dead from a sudden brain  aneurysm many fans were deeply upset  with showrunner Joss Whedon for killing  off Joyce  and they weren't the only ones even  Buffy herself Sarah Michelle Gellar  argued against the decision and I tried  so hard to talk about I was not happy  about it  although most fans now agree that the  body is one of the best episodes of the  entire series processing Joyce's death  definitely took some time and a lot of  tears lane Pryce Mad Men despite signs  throughout season 5 of Mad Men that Lane  was struggling with some heavy stuff his  suicide was still one of the most  upsetting moments in Sterling Cooper  history the ad man played by Jared  Harris had embezzled $1700 from the  agency to cover a debt a crime that Don  Draper discovers in despair Blaine  returns to the agency types of  resignation letter and hangs himself I  think something's terribly wrong with  mr. Pryce's office the distraught  reactions of lanes co-workers mirror  those of fans who were devastated to see  their favorite character meet such a  tragic untimely end Derek Shepherd  Grey's Anatomy  the doctor known as McDreamy was central  to this shondaland drama particularly  his rocky relationship with fellow doc  Meredith Grey but just when the couple  looked like they'd live happily ever  after a car accident leaves Derek brain  dead Meredith has to make the difficult  decision to remove him from life support  a plot twist that left many fans wanting  to pull the plug themselves under  televisions  [Music]  I am Colonel Blake mash and this  light-hearted comedy series the sudden  and unexpected death of Lieutenant  Colonel Blake in the third season was  unprecedented when actor McLean  Stevenson decided to leave the series  the show's creators wrote Blake off with  an honorable discharge only to cap the  episode with a devastating epilogue  Finlay Blake's plane was shot down over  the Sea of Japan the show received over  a thousand letters from viewers who  didn't appreciate this incredibly  depressing moment in a show that was  supposed to be funny  and they weren't alone the networks were  so upset about the scene CBS even cut it  entirely in later airings of the episode  Jax teller  Sons of Anarchy in the 2014 series  finale of Sons of Anarchy the antihero  played by Charlie Hunnam made a  controversial exit from the show and the  mortal plane by fleeing from the police  right into the path of an oncoming  18-wheeler Jax's suicide didn't sit well  with fans some thought he deserved  better and others thought he deserved  worse but above all everyone thought  that the computer-generated crows and  the final shots look completely  ridiculous  dan Connor Roseanne in the final season  of the long-running sitcom Roseanne  things take a turn for the weird the  Connor family wins the Illinois Lottery  Roseanne goes on Jerry Springer  dan has an affair and my writing is  really what got me through the last year  after Dan died I mean at first I felt so  betrayed as if he had left me for  another woman  wait what as it turns out dan is dead  killed by a heart attack at Darlene's  wedding and the crazy fantasies of  season 9 were just Roseanne's 